    "A reading is flagged once it sits more than %@ standard deviations from your own baseline, built from your %@ earlier readings. You are never compared with anyone else. Pausing uses its own rule instead, because a pause ratio near zero makes standard deviations misleading.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A reading is flagged once it sits more than %@ standard deviations from your own baseline, built from your %@ earlier readings. You are never compared with anyone else. Pausing uses its own rule instead, because a pause ratio near zero makes standard deviations misleading."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Se marca un cambio si una lectura se aleja más de %@ desviaciones estándar de tu referencia, calculada con tus %@ lecturas anteriores. Nunca se te compara con otras personas. Las pausas usan otra regla: cerca de cero, las desviaciones estándar pueden confundir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A short code to find this phrase fast.": {
