    "Closer to zero is more likely. The three terms are added, not multiplied, because they are logs — that is what keeps the numbers from underflowing.": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Closer to zero is more likely. The three terms are added, not multiplied, because they are logs — that is what keeps the numbers from underflowing."
          }
        },
        "es": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Más cerca de cero significa más probable. Se suman los tres valores porque son logaritmos; así los números no se vuelven demasiado pequeños."
          }
        }
      }
